# Root (rootmoi) chezmoiignore -- TRUE safe-by-default whitelist.
#
# Only the exact paths below are ever managed; everything else is ignored,
# so the root invocation can never touch an unrelated /etc file, including
# any file added to this source later without an explicit `!` line here.
#
# Syntax (verified against chezmoi v2.71.1): once a directory is ignored,
# its children cannot be re-included, so we re-include each directory level
# by name, then ignore its children, then re-include the exact managed files:
#
#   /*                   ignore every top-level entry
#   !portage/            re-include the portage dir (by name, not `!*/`)
#   portage/*            ignore portage's immediate children and their subtrees
#   !portage/env/        re-include the env subdir
#   portage/env/*        ignore env's children
#   !portage/env/allow-network   re-include one managed file
#
# When P4.1 adds a live /etc file to the source, it MUST gain a matching `!`
# line at every directory level plus the file itself, or it silently will not
# apply.  A decoy file with no `!` line is ignored (verified).
